I have made only one modification to the tests you added.
You included a test to ensure that no query is made when the cursor moves out from the edge of the brackets, but when functions are nested, a query is still necessary. Therefore, similar to other patterns, a query should be made when the nearest brackets change. For this reason, I have removed only this test.

### Deleted test that you added yesterday
```rust
// When moving to the edge of the bracket, clear the pop-up and query nothing.
let _not_used =
    cx.handle_request::<lsp::request::SignatureHelpRequest, _, _>(move |_, _, _| async move {
        panic!("Unexpected call to signature help");
    });
cx.set_state(indoc! {"
    fn main() {
        sample()ˇ;
    }
    fn sample(param1: u8, param2: u8) {}
"});
cx.editor(|editor, _| {
    assert!(editor.signature_help_state.as_ref().is_none());
});
```

### A nested function example
```rust
function1(a, b, function2()ˇ, 3)
```
---
Additionally, you added a test to ensure that the `signature_help_popover` is dismissed when multiple characters are selected. The test was failing, so I modified the implementation to pass this test. Specifically, I added a dedicated check flag to determine if the popover was hidden due to selection. This change ensures that all the tests you added now pass.

